      "program_name": "Affordable housing in-lieu fee fund and impact fee waivers for 100% affordable developments",
      "administering_agency": "San Benito County Resource Management Agency, Planning and Building; County Executive Office (impact fee program)",
      "funding_type": "fee waiver",
      "typical_award_size": "Section 21.03.012 (as amended December 13, 2022) allows in-lieu fees to fund an affordable housing trust and to reimburse the County for impact fee waivers granted to developments that are 100% affordable. Fee balance and any waiver approvals were not published in the 2026 Board agendas; the FY 2024-25 Annual Development Impact Fee Report (adopted January 13, 2026) covers the County's public facilities impact fee funds administered since the late 1980s. Historic voluntary affordable housing fees were $4,500 per market-rate unit.",
      "per_unit_cap": "Not published.",
      "affordability_requirement": "Waiver reimbursement applies only to 100% affordable developments; trust fund uses follow Chapter 21.03.",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "homeownership"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "No NOFA. Request an impact fee waiver with the entitlement application and confirm the in-lieu fund balance with Planning and Building; the County has not issued a housing fund NOFA.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "false",
      "layering_notes": "San Benito County is a small non-entitlement county with no housing department: the Resource Management Agency (Planning and Building, Abraham Prado, (831) 637-5313) administers the inclusionary ordinance, in-lieu fees, density bonus and TEFRA hearings; the Health and Human Services Agency (Community Services and Workforce Development) runs HHAP, the shelter and the Migrant Center; Behavioral Health holds BHSA; and the Housing Authority of the County of Santa Cruz administers vouchers and PBVs for Hollister and San Juan Bautista. The County has no HOME or CDBG entitlement, no housing trust fund NOFA and no County loan program; Hollister runs its own PLHA and CDBG programs (Pass 3). sanbenitocountyca.gov and the amlegal code library block automated access, so records were built from Board of Supervisors packets on cosb.granicus.com (attachments on d2kbkoa27fdvtw.cloudfront.net), HCD allocation tables and hacosantacruz.org. Confirmation needed: the ordinance language creating the waiver reimbursement was read in the 2022 Board packet, but the current code text, the fund balance and any adopted waiver procedure could not be opened (sanbenitocountyca.gov and amlegal 403). Treat as a negotiable cost reduction for a 100% affordable project rather than a funded program.",
      "source_url": "https://d2kbkoa27fdvtw.cloudfront.net/cosb/6404819104d9eef39ad033a9e4860b430.pdf",
      "record_id": "623a7bb988",
      "cycle_notes": "",
      "eligible_project_detail": [
        "100% affordable rental or ownership developments in unincorporated San Benito County"
      ],
      "next_deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_check": "no_date"
    }
