      "program_name": "Local Tenant Preference Ordinance (Chapter 21.04, Ordinance 1085)",
      "administering_agency": "San Benito County Resource Management Agency, Planning and Building",
      "funding_type": "other",
      "typical_award_size": "Not a subsidy: adopted October 14, 2025 under the Local Tenant Preferences to Prevent Displacement Act (Government Code 7061). Preferences for displaced San Benito County residents, neighborhood residents, local workers and school district employees, households with high housing costs, families with children in a local school district, agricultural employees, seniors and persons with disabilities. Applies to projects of five or more units, projects restricted to lower-income households, projects receiving County development assistance, and affordable units produced under Chapter 21.03.",
      "per_unit_cap": "Not applicable.",
      "affordability_requirement": "Applies to income-restricted units; written to be compatible with LIHTC and tax-exempt bond (IRC 142(d)) projects as permitted by Government Code 7061.",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "new construction",
        "acquisition-rehab"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "In effect; the preference must be written into tenant selection plans for any affordable project in unincorporated San Benito County and should be cleared with CTCAC and lenders early.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "false",
      "layering_notes": "San Benito County is a small non-entitlement county with no housing department: the Resource Management Agency (Planning and Building, Abraham Prado, (831) 637-5313) administers the inclusionary ordinance, in-lieu fees, density bonus and TEFRA hearings; the Health and Human Services Agency (Community Services and Workforce Development) runs HHAP, the shelter and the Migrant Center; Behavioral Health holds BHSA; and the Housing Authority of the County of Santa Cruz administers vouchers and PBVs for Hollister and San Juan Bautista. The County has no HOME or CDBG entitlement, no housing trust fund NOFA and no County loan program; Hollister runs its own PLHA and CDBG programs (Pass 3). sanbenitocountyca.gov and the amlegal code library block automated access, so records were built from Board of Supervisors packets on cosb.granicus.com (attachments on d2kbkoa27fdvtw.cloudfront.net), HCD allocation tables and hacosantacruz.org. The ordinance was developed by the Board's Housing Policy Reform Ad Hoc Committee with the San Benito High School District, which wants workforce housing for teachers; developers should expect the County to ask for school employee and local worker preferences in any affordable housing agreement. Source is the October 14, 2025 Board packet (second reading); first reading September 9, 2025.",
      "source_url": "https://d2kbkoa27fdvtw.cloudfront.net/cosb/5c4660a27183c9887503123de21939ea0.pdf",
      "record_id": "b9d8d23246",
