      "next_deadline": "No County NOFA. Confirm the County's 2024-2028 PLHA plan activities with the County Executive Office; allocations this small are typically spent on services.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "false",
      "layering_notes": "San Benito County is a small non-entitlement county with no housing department: the Resource Management Agency (Planning and Building, Abraham Prado, (831) 637-5313) administers the inclusionary ordinance, in-lieu fees, density bonus and TEFRA hearings; the Health and Human Services Agency (Community Services and Workforce Development) runs HHAP, the shelter and the Migrant Center; Behavioral Health holds BHSA; and the Housing Authority of the County of Santa Cruz administers vouchers and PBVs for Hollister and San Juan Bautista. The County has no HOME or CDBG entitlement, no housing trust fund NOFA and no County loan program; Hollister runs its own PLHA and CDBG programs (Pass 3). sanbenitocountyca.gov and the amlegal code library block automated access, so records were built from Board of Supervisors packets on cosb.granicus.com (attachments on d2kbkoa27fdvtw.cloudfront.net), HCD allocation tables and hacosantacruz.org. Confirmation needed: the County's own PLHA five-year plan and its use of the 2024 and 2025 allocations were not found in the 2026 Board agendas (the 'Resolution 2026-06 Adopt PLHA Plan' attachment on the March 24, 2026 item is the City of San Juan Bautista's resolution). At roughly $125,000 a year the County allocation cannot anchor a development loan. Source is the March 24, 2026 Board packet; allocation figures from HCD's 2024-2028 PLHA NOFA tables.",
